# The formatting commands in HTML mode. What the editor holds is read back as Markdown
# ("markdown-is"), which shows the formatting in text.

== Ctrl+B makes the selection bold
modes: html
text: one two three
caret: select "two"
keys: ^b
text-is: one two three
markdown-is: one **two** three

== Ctrl+B twice leaves it as it was
modes: html
text: one two three
caret: select "two"
keys: ^b
keys: ^b
markdown-is: one two three

== Ctrl+I makes the selection italic
modes: html
text: one two three
caret: select "two"
keys: ^i
markdown-is: one *two* three

== Ctrl+Shift+X strikes the selection through
modes: html
text: one two three
caret: select "two"
keys: ^+x
markdown-is: one ~~two~~ three

== Ctrl+B with nothing selected makes what is typed next bold
modes: html
type: "plain "
keys: ^b
type: bold
keys: ^b
type: " plain"
markdown-is: plain **bold** plain

== Ctrl+Alt+2 makes the paragraph a heading
modes: html
text: one two three
caret: after "one"
keys: ^%2
text-is: one two three
caret-is: after "one"
typing-works
markdown-is: ## one two three

== Ctrl+Alt+2 again takes the heading off
modes: html
text: one two three
caret: after "one"
keys: ^%2
keys: ^%2
markdown-is: one two three

== Ctrl+Alt+0 makes a heading normal text
modes: html
markdown: ## Title
caret: after "Ti"
keys: ^%0
markdown-is: Title

== Making a paragraph a quote keeps its bold words
modes: html
markdown: one **two** three
caret: after "one"
keys: ^+9
markdown-is: > one **two** three

== Ctrl+Shift+9 on a quote takes it out of the quote
modes: html
markdown: > one two
caret: after "one"
keys: ^+9
markdown-is: one two

== Ctrl+Shift+L makes a bullet and again takes it off
modes: html
text: one
caret: end
keys: ^+l
markdown-is: - one
keys: ^+l
markdown-is: one

== Ctrl+Shift+N makes a numbered item
modes: html
text: one
caret: end
keys: ^+n
markdown-is: 1. one

== Ctrl+Space clears formatting
modes: html
markdown: ## one **two** three
caret: select "one two three"
keys: ^{SPACE}
markdown-is: one two three

== Ctrl+K puts in a link and typing afterwards is not part of it
modes: html
type: "See "
keys: ^k
wait: 1.5
front-is: Insert Link
type: https://example.com/page
keys: {TAB}
type: the site
keys: {ENTER}
wait: 1.2
front-is: New Message
focus-is: Message body
type: " now"
markdown-is: See [the site](https://example.com/page) now

== Ctrl+T reports formatting and leaves the caret and focus alone
modes: html
text: one two three
caret: after "one"
keys: ^t
wait: 0.8
caret-is: after "one"
typing-works

== Undo takes back a formatting command
modes: html
text: one two three
caret: select "two"
keys: ^b
keys: ^z
markdown-is: one two three
